  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> be two non singular matrices of same order such that <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></math> for consecutive positive integral values of <math><mi>k</mi></math>, then <math><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is equal to",
